            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is no way to underestimate the importance of the countless ways that ethics impacts case managers and the patients we serve. In fact, solid ethical decisions are such an integral part of case management practice that the Commission for Case Manager Certification has increased its number of continuing education units required for recertification. Discussion and resources are outlined in the Editorial.</AbstractText>
